<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  Ikee_Rename.xml                           Jawa_Patches - new file 2026-08-20
  ============================================================================

  The eyeling becomes the IKEE. Owner's ruling 2026-08-15: "AA_Eyeling MUST be
  made into a star-wars-style pet for the starting Jawa clan to keep!"
  Design is settled in SCENARIO_SPEC.md, section "The ikee".

  The name is from the canon Jawaese "Ikee ikee!" - the cry a Jawa gives on
  spotting something worth taking. It pairs with the ship: the Utinni is named
  for the find, the ikee for the looking.

  🔴 RENAME AND PLACE ONLY. THE ART IS UNTOUCHED and so is every stat. The
  animal was checked field by field and is already right for this campaign -
  ComfyTemperatureMax 60 is built for the dune sea, foodType
  OmnivoreRoughAnimal needs no crops on a clan forbidden from sowing, and
  trainability Intermediate is what makes it a pet. ⛔ Do not touch wildness,
  baseBodySize, foodType, trainability or any stat. The IDENTITY changes; the
  animal does not.

  ============================================================================
  🔴 THE ITEM'S XML WARNING IS BACKWARDS, exactly as it was for the ash storms
  ============================================================================
  The queue item says:

      🪤 `wildAnimals` is a LIST of
         <li><animal>X</animal><commonality>N</commonality></li>
         - NOT the dictionary shorthand.

  Read `BiomeAnimalRecord` instead:

      public void LoadDataFromXmlCustom(XmlNode xmlRoot)
      {
          DirectXmlCrossRefLoader.RegisterObjectWantsCrossRef(this, "animal", xmlRoot);
          commonality = ParseHelper.FromString<float>(xmlRoot.FirstChild.Value);
      }

  It takes the NODE NAME as the animal and the node's TEXT as the commonality,
  so `<AA_Eyeling>N</AA_Eyeling>` is the only form that loads. The `<li>` form
  the item calls mandatory would take FirstChild of an element and misparse.
  This is the SAME class as WeatherCommonalityRecord, and the same warning was
  wrong there too - both were written from the biomeConfigs/FactionDef lesson,
  which is a real trap but a DIFFERENT one. ⇒ Check the record class; do not
  generalise from another field's shape.

  ⚠️ AND `wildAnimals` TAKES A PawnKindDef, NOT THE ThingDef. Races_Eyeling.xml
  declares AA_Eyeling TWICE - a ThingDef and a PawnKindDef sharing the defName,
  which is what the item flagged and it was right to. The biome entries below
  resolve to the PAWNKIND.

  ⚠️ VERSION FOLDER: the item cites the mod's 1.5 copy. Alpha Animals ships 1.5
  AND 1.6 and the 1.6 one is what loads. Both were read; the fields agree.

  ============================================================================
  PLACEMENT - three biomes, and the exclusions are deliberate
  ============================================================================
    Wasteland          1.2   main range
    ExtremeDesert      0.5   sparse
    ZBiome_DesertOasis 0.8   uncommon

  🔴 NOT THE NIGHTSIDE. The shipped ComfyTemperatureRange is 0 to 60 C, so an
  ikee freezes there. Not in Ocean or Lake, not in the wet biomes.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Alpha Animals</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- The ThingDef: what the player reads on the animal itself. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Eyeling"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>ikee</label></value>
        </li>

        <!-- The PawnKindDef shares the defName and also ships label "eyeling".
             Renaming only the ThingDef would leave the old name showing wherever
             the kind's label is used. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="AA_Eyeling"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>ikee</label></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="AA_Eyeling"]/description</xpath>
          <value>
            <description>A single great eye walking on soft tentacles, warm to the touch and blind to nothing. The clans keep them because an ikee sees the glint of buried metal long before a Jawa does - and because a people known across the desert by their own glowing eyes cannot help but read one as a good omen. It eats what the waste offers.</description>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="Wasteland"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
          <value><AA_Eyeling>1.2</AA_Eyeling></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ExtremeDesert"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
          <value><AA_Eyeling>0.5</AA_Eyeling></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_DesertOasis"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
          <value><AA_Eyeling>0.8</AA_Eyeling></value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
